# Commit after every change

After finishing a coherent unit of work (feature, fix, copy change, refactor), create a git commit before stopping or moving on.

- Do not wait to be asked again — the user requested commits after every change.
- Follow the repo's normal commit protocol: status, diff, log style, stage relevant files, commit via HEREDOC, verify with status.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials). Never update git config. Do not push unless asked.
- Prefer focused commits that match the change just made (not giant catch-up dumps when avoidable).
